---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'
---
<SiteLayout title="Benchmarks" path="benchmarks" description="Nova's benchmark methodology and the honest current absence of comparative performance results.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">No comparative results yet</span>
      <h1>Measure, then claim.</h1>
      <p>Nova has no published Rust/Go/C++/Python benchmark comparison. This page states that plainly and defines the methodology that must be followed before any number appears in marketing.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 24px;">
    <div class="wrap grid-2" style="align-items: start;">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="notice danger"><strong>Do not cite this page as evidence of performance parity.</strong> The compiler is an early vertical slice using a new runtime and checked arithmetic. No representative suite exists.</p>
        <h2>What is verified</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><code>cargo test --workspace</code> passes across the Rust bootstrap: lexer, parser, sema, package, LSP, native codegen and the browser front end.</li>
          <li>Native executables are built through LLVM/Clang and executed in codegen tests.</li>
          <li>Studio typecheck and production build pass.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>These are correctness/build facts, not throughput or latency measurements.</p>
        <h2>Required methodology</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Identical algorithms, input sizes, correctness checks and compiler flags across languages.</li>
          <li>Release builds, documented compiler/runtime versions and hardware.</li>
          <li>Warmups and at least 30 samples; report median, p95, peak RSS and binary size.</li>
          <li>Separate compile time, process startup and steady-state throughput.</li>
          <li>Publish losses and runtime/ARC costs, not only wins.</li>
          <li>Label checked versus unchecked code; never compare them as equivalent.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="kicker">Planned suites</div>
        <h3>Workloads, when implemented</h3>
        <table class="status-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Suite</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Integer loops</td><td><span class="badge planned">planned</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Recursive calls</td><td><span class="badge planned">planned</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Sorting</td><td><span class="badge planned">planned</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>String processing</td><td><span class="badge planned">planned</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Hash maps</td><td><span class="badge planned">blocked on Map</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>JSON / file IO</td><td><span class="badge planned">planned</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Concurrency</td><td><span class="badge planned">not implemented</span></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
